# Shell scripts MUST keep LF endings.
#
# These run under WSL/bash. Git on Windows checked them out as CRLF after they
# were first committed, and bash then failed with `$'\r': command not found`
# before the build could start — a two-hour build that never began. eol=lf is
# what stops that happening to the next person who clones this on Windows.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for anything else consumed by a Unix toolchain.
gradlew text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
